# Panel Shop Demo Guide

Bench: https://jasonx12345.github.io/Demo_V2/
Lead Hand: https://jasonx12345.github.io/Demo_V2/priority.html
TV board: https://jasonx12345.github.io/Demo_V2/board.html

Use the same browser profile for a simple two-window demo. For separate devices, follow the Shared records section below. All names, jobs and material records are fabricated.

## Demo badges

| Badge | Name | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 4471 | A. Kovach | Technician |
| 5104 | R. Bissonnette | Technician |
| 3218 | J. Okafor | Lead |
| 2907 | M. Cardoso | Lead |

Reset restores fabricated fixtures and signs out. Serial/WO/finding/receipt counters retain their high-water marks. Existing progress migrates; previously complete stages are marked as migrated stage closures.

## New order, checklist and materials

1. Sign in as lead **3218**. Choose **New work order**, then **Fill demo example** or enter your own parent job, project, due date and panel rows. Each row accepts an alphanumeric rack and its own type, including Telecom.
2. Create drafts and open **Review draft**. Nothing has been completed. Drafts stay off the TV board.
3. Choose **Edit checklist**. Change this panel's rack, type and due date. Add/remove/reorder ordinary steps within a stage. Lead approval and Final QA review/release gates stay required.
4. Add two material lines: **AB-1756-24V**, power supply, quantity **2**; and **TB-6**, terminal block, quantity **6**. Save the draft revision.
5. Assign it to A. Kovach. **Release to shop** freezes the checklist revision. The shortages create red material holds.

## Receiving, wrong parts and hold clearance

1. Open **Scan receiving label** from the panel controls. Select the panel you just created.
2. **Load demo label** is fabricated and defaults to PNL-611: change the panel selection to your new panel if needed. Confirm part **AB-1756-24V**, quantity **2**, and save.
3. Return to the panel: the power-supply line is received, but TB-6 is still short and keeps the panel on hold.
4. Record an unlisted part to show that wrong parts do not satisfy the list. Then record **TB-6**, quantity **6**. The remaining automatic hold clears.
5. Begin work, switch to technician **4471**, open the panel and complete Receiving steps. It stays in Receiving until you select **Sign off Receiving stage**.
6. For a quick receiving-only story, use seeded **PNL-611**, which already has those two material requirements.

For real photos, crop around the label before uploading. Use a straight, sharp image and keep a margin around text/barcodes. The OCR engine preloads and caches models. Verify extracted fields. If needed, edit raw OCR text and select **Match fields again from text**. A receipt includes your badge, timestamp and work order. The photo itself stays in the browser.

## Stages and booked labour

1. Assembly: complete each step. Chassis torque **22** passes; busbar torque **35** passes. Step 7 needs approval by a lead different from its completer. After approval, explicitly **Sign off Assembly stage**.
2. Wiring: complete the steps; wire count **148** passes. Step 11 needs independent lead approval, then **Sign off Wiring stage**.
3. During any active, unheld stage, expand **Book labour**, enter minutes and a description. The dashboard/project hours reflect actual entries. Stage time and time on hold are separate.
4. Expand **Place a hold**, describe a missing item/quantity and expected arrival date. Work is blocked. A lead clears it with a reason. Show it at the top of the priority list and TV board.

Seeded **PNL-602** starts in Wiring and is a useful shortcut. Complete its remaining Wiring checks, get the independent approval, and explicitly sign off the stage. Stage completion is now always a separate action.

## Failed test and rework

1. In Testing, complete continuity, then enter insulation resistance **1** (below the required minimum **100**). Completing that failed reading records it, creates a finding and returns the panel to Wiring.
2. Open the report: the rework cycle retains previous Wiring/Testing results, the failed reading, names, timestamps and approvals.
3. Repeat Wiring, its lead approval and stage signoff, then repeat Testing with passing values. Qualitative failures can be entered through **Record failed test / return to Wiring** with a reason.
4. A lead dispositions the failure finding after corrections and retesting. Final QA remains blocked until open findings are dispositioned.

## Final QA and PDF

1. Complete the visual inspection and findings review.
2. Complete Final QA release, then switch to a different lead for its independent approval.
3. A lead selects **Sign off Final QA stage**. The panel becomes Complete, moves to the bottom of the priority dashboard and leaves the TV list.
4. Open **Build report** and **Save / Print PDF**. Choose Save as PDF. The report includes material requirements and receipts, holds, stage approvals, rework cycles, labour, findings and history.

Seeded **PNL-601** is a shortcut for Final QA. Disposition its label-alignment finding first.

## Morning meeting and assignments

Open the Lead Hand priority dashboard while signed in as a lead. Review holds at the top, then contract deadlines, stalled builds and bottlenecks. Assign a technician. On the bench, switch to that technician and select **My assigned panels**. The TV uses the same ordered list and refreshes every five seconds. Demo bottleneck/stalled thresholds are shown on the dashboard.

## Shared records on separate devices

The public GitHub Pages demo is standalone unless connected to a separate shared server. To demonstrate phone/laptop/TV synchronization on the same network:

1. Start the included Node server using **npm start**. For LAN access set HOST to 0.0.0.0 before starting it (PowerShell: $env:HOST='0.0.0.0').
2. Open the website from that computer's LAN URL on every device, for example http://192.168.1.20:8766/. Use that same address for the bench, /priority.html and /board.html.
3. Expand **Shared demo connection** at the bottom of each page. Enter that server URL and connect. Connecting loads the server's records; the first browser initializes an empty server. Your badge remains local to your device.
4. Record a receipt or sign off a stage on one device. The others update within roughly three seconds. The server retains records across restarts.
5. If two devices save at once, the stale save is rejected and local records are preserved. **Reload shared records** explicitly loads the server version before continuing; reapply desired local changes afterwards.

This is a fabricated-data demo server with no production authentication. Public HTTPS hosting and authentication still need a hosting destination. GitHub Pages alone does not provide the shared database. For LAN demonstrations serve the full site from the Node server, rather than connecting an HTTPS GitHub page to a private HTTP endpoint.

## Current boundaries

SQL/office-system retrieval remains future work. Actual shop-specific checklist content and warning thresholds need confirmation. The website supports manual material requirements and actual labour booking, but has no purchasing, payroll or job-costing integration. Barcode decoding depends on browser support; the receiving OCR workflow still works without it.


Batch creation: on New work order, enter **Panel quantity** and **Starting rack**, then select **Generate panel rows**. Numeric rack portions increment (201A, 202A, 203A); review each row and set its own panel type before creating drafts. No leading zeros are added.
